      "language": "zh+en",
      "prompt": "A. These are supplied fictional calculations, not a source paper's implementation. A binary classifier has true-class probability q=sigmoid(z), l(q)=-log(q), and a(q)=(1-q)^2. Compare training with L(q)=a(q)l(q), differentiating the full expression, against evaluating the same a(q) on the forward pass but stopping its gradient. Derive both derivatives with respect to q and z at q=1/2, retaining exact log(2) terms. Does matching the coefficient value or freezing an unrelated weighting network make the parameter updates identical? Distinguish class-dependent factors, confidence-dependent factors and an overall objective coefficient. Report whether this version's bank has a matched two-source record for class factors in classification log-loss terms, versus an entire ordinary weighted-cross-entropy loss or a full adaptive-loss mechanism. Use actual available records, scopes and unresolved source conflicts, not title matches. Does an incomplete admission entry prohibit a valid weighted loss or an author-defined new component?",
